7592186252859 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252859 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186251644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252859 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1d67c074-de3d-5624-a3d0-a52f941600ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253059 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186250876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253059 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186251295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253059 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186252053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253059 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186252304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253059 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186252618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253059 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253059 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253059 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186250876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253059 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "92e60e35-c089-5683-b48c-03659e05f5af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253501 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186253059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253501 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118755" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253501 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253501 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $f(x)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+4}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is convergent\n- ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is divergent\n- ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is divergent" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253501 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "260fa3cd-f59d-50c6-a56e-8cfbd29393f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253501 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an improper integral in which both the left and right endpoints are unbounded:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nIf the integrand $f(x)$ is continuous on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ then we can break the integral up into two improper integrals, each with a single unbounded endpoint:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we can compute each of the two integrals separately and combine their results. \n\n**Watch out!** If either of the two integrals on the right-hand side is divergent, then the integral on the left-hand side is also divergent.\n\nFirst, we calculate the antiderivative using a substitution.  Let $u={x}^{2}+4$,  then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x.$ Hence, the antiderivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's evaluate each integral in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the required integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4))|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({a}^{2}+4)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{ln}⁡({a}^{2}+4)-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs $a\\to \\infty $, we have that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({a}^{2}+4)\\to \\infty .$ So the integral diverges.\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the required integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4))|}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({a}^{2}+4)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{2}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{ln}⁡({a}^{2}+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs $a\\to -\\infty $, we have that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({a}^{2}+4)\\to \\infty .$ So the integral diverges.\n\n- Statement III is true. The integral in statement III can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHowever, both integrals on the right-hand side are divergent. Therefore, the integral on the left-hand side is also divergent.\n\nIn conclusion,  only statements II and III are true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253528 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186252859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253528 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118976" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253528 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253528 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/dc/dcd36221e7ad293f0aac1ab99ece80641cb077efd05adc168a552e97d86100c8.png)\n\nIn parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AD}=\\overset{\\to }{CB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AD}+\\overset{\\to }{DF}=\\overset{\\to }{FA}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253528 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "41da8ad0-e0fc-5f39-8eb7-c4706c551e5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253528 #edb/ref 1074 "- Equality I is false. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{AD}\\ne \\overset{\\to }{CB}$ since they have the opposite directions.\n\n- Equality II is true. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}.$\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{AD}+\\overset{\\to }{DF}=\\overset{\\to }{AF}\\ne \\overset{\\to }{FA}$ since they have the opposite directions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253819 #edb/ref 1080 "5\\,040" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253819 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253819 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "111b2cfd-82b0-5772-b24e-fd1bd23e4b33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253831 #edb/ref 1080 "132" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253831 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253831 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "127ab74a-78a9-50ff-b775-392162c822af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253963 #edb/ref 1080 "7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253963 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253963 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "21171d16-53d1-5b90-a331-d3226cde70e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
